{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Python code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Python 3 code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Python 3 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\ndef main():\n    turnNum = int(input())\n    # choices include rock, scissor, paper respectively\n    aliceChoices = list(map(int, input().split(' ')))\n    bobChoices = list(map(int, input().split(' ')))\n    \n    bobChoices.append(bobChoices.pop(0))\n    minWin, maxWin = [0, 0]\n    \n    # calculate the maximum number of rounds Alice can win\n    for i, choice in enumerate(aliceChoices):\n        maxWin += min([choice, bobChoices[i]])\n        \n    # calculate the minimum number of rounds Alice can win\n    maximum = max(bobChoices)\n    for i, choice in enumerate(bobChoices):\n        if choice == maximum and choice + aliceChoices[i] > minWin:\n            minWin = choice + aliceChoices[i]\n    maximum = max(aliceChoices)\n    for i, choice in enumerate(aliceChoices):\n        if choice == maximum and choice + bobChoices[i] > minWin:\n            minWin = choice + bobChoices[i]\n    minWin = minWin - turnNum if minWin > turnNum else 0\n    print(f'{minWin} {maxWin}')\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    main()\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "openai/gpt-oss-20b"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {\n        java.io.BufferedReader br = new java.io.BufferedReader(new java.io.InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        int turnNum = Integer.parseInt(br.readLine().trim());\n\n        StringTokenizer st = new StringTokenizer(br.readLine());\n        int[] alice = new int[turnNum];\n        for (int i = 0; i < turnNum; i++) {\n            alice[i] = Integer.parseInt(st.nextToken());\n        }\n\n        st = new StringTokenizer(br.readLine());\n        int[] bob = new int[turnNum];\n        for (int i = 0; i < turnNum; i++) {\n            bob[i] = Integer.parseInt(st.nextToken());\n        }\n\n        // Rotate bob's choices left by one\n        int firstBob = bob[0];\n        for (int i = 0; i < turnNum - 1; i++) {\n            bob[i] = bob[i + 1];\n        }\n        bob[turnNum - 1] = firstBob;\n\n        int maxWin = 0;\n        for (int i = 0; i < turnNum; i++) {\n            maxWin += Math.min(alice[i], bob[i]);\n        }\n\n        int minWin = 0;\n        int maxBob = java.util.Arrays.stream(bob).max().getAsInt();\n        for (int i = 0; i < turnNum; i++) {\n            if (bob[i] == maxBob) {\n                int sum = bob[i] + alice[i];\n                if (sum > minWin) {\n                    minWin = sum;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n\n        int maxAlice = java.util.Arrays.stream(alice).max().getAsInt();\n        for (int i = 0; i < turnNum; i++) {\n            if (alice[i] == maxAlice) {\n                int sum = alice[i] + bob[i];\n                if (sum > minWin) {\n                    minWin = sum;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n\n        if (minWin > turnNum) {\n            minWin -= turnNum;\n        } else {\n            minWin = 0;\n        }\n\n        System.out.println(minWin + \" \" + maxWin);\n    }\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</